<!--
    A findable tag that Apple did not make - a Chipolo, a Pebblebee, anything paired into the
    network by somebody else.

    **Deliberately not Apple's Find My mark.** That is their branding, and shipping it in an app
    that already tells Apple's servers it is an iPhone is not a fight worth picking. Concentric
    arcs radiating from a point say "this broadcasts and can be found" without borrowing anything.

    Tinted at the point of use, like apple.xml.
-->
